Leave the Docker engine client out of the wasip1 build.

Reason: bufremoteplugindocker's client pulls in github.com/moby/moby/client
and docker/go-connections, whose Unix-socket code does not compile for
wasip1 (syscall.RawSockaddrUnix, syscall.ForkLock). Only `buf beta registry
plugin push` uses it, and that needs a local Docker daemon, which SLICC
does not have. docker.go builds everywhere except wasip1; docker_wasip1.go
keeps the package's types and options and returns "buf on wasip1 cannot
reach a Docker engine" from NewClient. This also keeps moby out of buf.wasm.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: buf compiles for wasip1 with its Docker client, or drops it.

